            "description": "# Signature Video Summary\nSignature Video Summary is a Python package that generates video summaries using the signature transform. It extracts keyframes from a video and creates a summary based on the minimum standard deviation of the root mean square error (RMSE) between the frames' signature transform.\n\n## Installation\nTo install the package, first ensure you have Python 3.6 or higher installed on your system. Then, run the following command:\n\n\npip install .[ffmpeg]\n\nNote that this package requires the ffmpeg binary to be installed on your system. You can find installation instructions for various platforms in the official FFmpeg documentation.\n\n## Usage\nYou can use the Signature Video Summary package in your Python scripts or from the command line.\n\n\nfrom signature_video_summary import summarize_video\n\ninput_video = \"path/to/your/video.mp4\"\nsummary_length = 27\nsummary_n = 10\nfps = 1\n\nsummarize_video(input_video, summary_length, summary_n, fps)\n\n\n## Command line\npython -m signature_video_summary path/to/your/video.mp4 -l 27 -n 10 -f 1\n\nArguments\ninput_video: Path to the input video file (.mp4).\n-l or --summary_length: Length of the summary (default: 27).\n-n or --summary_n: Number of summary iterations (default: 10).\n-f or --fps: Frames per second to sample from the input video (default: 1).\n\n## License\nThis project is licensed under the MIT License. See the LICENSE file for details.\n",
